            "review_title": "Review at Banh Cuon Ba Hanh",
            "review_text": "Brian L\n151 contributions\n0\nOH! Wrong pick!\nJan 2019 • Family\nA cafe shop rather than a restaurant, Just supply ready made food which is only a kind of fast food standard. \nPretty misleading If reading the reviews.\nWritten January 20, 2019\nBanh Cuon Ba Hanh\nDear Brian;\n\nBanh Cuon Ba Hanh is steamed rice cake made of rice paste, with rice soaked up in water for 4h and then ground 3 times before moulding it and then paste onto steam over hot pot. After that it is wrapped up with mushroom, pork, onion and served hot with dipping fish sauce. What seemed to us that you posted a picture with lemongrass rolls. This is also hand made using lemongrass and combination hatched porks then roasted. It is not ready nor fast food. It is not mis leading review but you made wrong order by not ordering the steamed rice cake.\n\nBest wishes\nBanh Cuon Ba Hanh\nRead more\nWritten October 26, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
